%I A398235 #13 Jul 26 2026 21:17:40
%S A398235 491923,491951,491969,491983,664036843,664036853,664036859,664036963,
%T A398235 664037173,664037177,664037203,664037207,664037243,664037281,
%U A398235 664037321,664037383,664037443,664037971,664037993,664037999,664038017,664038047,664038217,664038257,664038301
%N A398235 Primes p for which pi_{24;7,13}(p) - pi_{24;1,19}(p) = -1, where pi_{m;a,b,...}(x) is the number of primes <= x which are congruent to a or b or ... (mod m).
%C A398235 Let H be a proper subgroup of (Z/NZ)* containing all the squares, and S != H be a coset of H. Assuming the generalized Riemann hypothesis (GRH) and the Grand Simplicity Hypothesis (GSH; called LI in page 29 of Greg Martin's 2010 link), then pi_{N;S}(x) > pi_{N;H}(x) occurs more often than not: the set {pi_{N;S}(x) > pi_{N;H}(x)} has logarithmic density greater than 1/2. This phenomenon is called "Chebyshev's bias".
%C A398235 Here we have N = 24, H = {1,19} and S = {7,13}. There are 42440 known terms, among which a(35726..42440) = 480151933441-480313346399 are from a single sign-changing zone. No furthur terms up to p = 929349098281, for which pi_{24;7,13}(p) - pi_{24;1,19}(p) = 7581.
%H A398235 Jianing Song, <a href="/A398235/b398235.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..42440</a>
%H A398235 Greg Martin and Daniel Fiorilli, <a href="https://personal.math.ubc.ca/~gerg/slides/Chennai-31Aug10.pdf">Prime number races: An asymptotic formula for the densities</a>, Analytic and Combinatorial Number Theory, Institute of Mathematical Sciences, Chennai, India. August 31, 2010.
%H A398235 Greg Martin, <a href="https://personal.math.ubc.ca/~gerg/slides/Canberra-29Nov18.pdf">Prime number races</a>, Pure Math Seminar, UNSW Canberra. November 29, 2018.
%H A398235 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chebyshev%27s_bias">Chebyshev's bias</a>.
%o A398235 (PARI) my(k=0); forprime(p=2, 1e11, if(p%24==1||p%24==19, k--); if(p%24==7||p%24==13, k++); if(k==-1, print1(p, ", ")))
%Y A398235 Cf. other races between cosets of index 4 in (Z/24Z)*: A295354 (between {1,17} and {7,23}), A297448 (between {1,17} and {5,13}), A380877 (between {1,13} and {7,19}), A398234, A398236.
%K A398235 nonn,new
%O A398235 1,1
%A A398235 _Jianing Song_, Jul 24 2026
